## Code Blocks

```javascript
function greet(name) {
  console.log(`Hello, ${name}!`);
}

greet("World");
```

```python
def fibonacci(n: int) -> list[int]:
    sequence = [0, 1]

    while len(sequence) < n:
        sequence.append(sequence[-1] + sequence[-2])

    return sequence[:n]


print(fibonacci(10))
```

```json
{
  "name": "Noted",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "markdown": true,
  "features": ["preview", "syntax highlighting", "tables"]
}
```

```html
<article>
  <h1>Hello, Markdown!</h1>
  <p>This is HTML inside a code block.</p>
</article>
```

```css
:root {
  --background: #ffffff;
  --foreground: #171717;
}

body {
  background: var(--background);
  color: var(--foreground);
}
```

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Indented code block:

    const message = "Indented code";
    console.log(message);

## Tables

| Feature | Supported | Rating |
|:--------|:---------:|-------:|
| Headings | Yes | 10 |
| Tables | Yes | 9 |
| Footnotes | Maybe | 8 |
| Mermaid | Maybe | 7 |

Escaped pipe inside a table:

| Syntax | Output |
|---|---|
| `A \| B` | A \| B |
| `**Bold**` | **Bold** |

## Footnotes

Here is a sentence with a footnote.[^1]

Here is another footnote with a longer identifier.[^important-note]

An inline footnote may also work.^[This is an inline footnote.]

[^1]: This is the first footnote.

[^important-note]: This footnote contains multiple lines.

    It may also contain an indented paragraph or code.

